      "before": "### 3.1 `DependencySourceSetV1`",
      "after": "### 3.1 `DependencySourceSetV1`\n\n**NKC-1 prospective Rust package and prepared-owner key encoding.** The exact CONTRACT.md, recipes.json, native-key-codecs.schema.json and materialization-map.json under docs/implementation/m3/snapshot-plan-c/native-key-codec-r1/ select pkg1/rawSHA256C([name,version,sourceId]) within one admitted native context and own2/rawSHA256C([source,packageKey,snapshotManifestPathOrNull]) for new-M3 Rust prepared owners. Retain full closed witnesses and rederive before joins. Path owners require their actual sealed in-snapshot Cargo.toml locator; nonpath dependency owners require null; snapshot owners require path source. Exact current schema Unicode scalar bounds, canonical byte/depth/scalar restrictions and historical codec selections remain. Safe key spelling does not admit an owner, source, generated row or grant. This unit does not select workspace/activation producer mapping, physical acquisition/adapter/worker namespaces or provenance-aware failure composition; actual admission and complete R3, security library/harness, product, effectiveL/owner/GT/qualification gates stay open. Bound R3-MR1 and C-ENV1 remain closed and unchanged.\n"
    }
  ],
